WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.339
- Welcome back everybody.

00:00:01.339 --> 00:00:02.790
Jennifer Garner is here with us.

00:00:02.790 --> 00:00:03.623
Give it up.

00:00:03.623 --> 00:00:04.938
(audience cheering)

00:00:04.938 --> 00:00:05.880
Our next guest is an

00:00:05.880 --> 00:00:07.080
NFL Hall of Famer

00:00:07.080 --> 00:00:08.610
and you can see him every week on

00:00:08.610 --> 00:00:10.671
Thursday Night Football, on Prime Video.

00:00:10.671 --> 00:00:11.610
(swoosh sound)

00:00:11.610 --> 00:00:13.560
- It's shocking to me
that you were even able

00:00:13.560 --> 00:00:15.390
to play in this weather, but you did.

00:00:15.390 --> 00:00:16.830
What was the experience like here?

00:00:16.830 --> 00:00:18.300
- You know, coming out to the

00:00:18.300 --> 00:00:21.930
Frozen Tundra at Lambeau Field?

00:00:21.930 --> 00:00:23.550
I remember playing out here, but you do.

00:00:23.550 --> 00:00:24.780
I had everything on back then,

00:00:24.780 --> 00:00:26.040
but I remember looking,
I scored this touch

00:00:26.040 --> 00:00:27.180
and I was like, hey, I turned around and

00:00:27.180 --> 00:00:28.320
I'm telling that guy, don't touch me.

00:00:28.320 --> 00:00:30.630
Don't touch me, because that ground hurts.

00:00:30.630 --> 00:00:32.850
But honestly, I don't even
remember scoring this touch.

00:00:32.850 --> 00:00:35.039
That's how much the
cold gets into my mind.

00:00:35.039 --> 00:00:36.510
(audience cheering)

00:00:36.510 --> 00:00:39.141
- TNF coverage begins at
7:00 pm Eastern, tonight.

00:00:39.141 --> 00:00:41.468
Please welcome, Tony Gonzalez.

00:00:41.468 --> 00:00:42.738
(audience cheering)

00:00:42.738 --> 00:00:47.738
(upbeat music)

00:00:57.822 --> 00:00:59.769
(audience cheering)

00:00:59.769 --> 00:01:01.760
- Yeah.

00:01:01.760 --> 00:01:02.593
Alrighty.

00:01:02.593 --> 00:01:04.346
- Well, welcome to the show.

00:01:04.346 --> 00:01:07.350
So, from that video,
you are not into cold.

00:01:07.350 --> 00:01:08.217
You don't like being cold?

00:01:08.217 --> 00:01:09.240
- No, I hate the cold.

00:01:09.240 --> 00:01:10.110
I hate it.

00:01:10.110 --> 00:01:11.010
I'm a California boy.

00:01:11.010 --> 00:01:12.870
You know, I was born and
raised in California.

00:01:12.870 --> 00:01:14.940
Went to Berkeley, which was still nice.

00:01:14.940 --> 00:01:15.773
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:01:15.773 --> 00:01:16.882
And when I got drafted to Kansas City,

00:01:16.882 --> 00:01:19.170
I was not prepared for...
Like, I always called it,

00:01:19.170 --> 00:01:21.092
I have a condition, it's called Tropical.

00:01:21.092 --> 00:01:22.580
(people laughing)

00:01:22.580 --> 00:01:24.019
I like tropical weather.

00:01:24.019 --> 00:01:26.370
Warm... but I get, it gets to my bones.

00:01:26.370 --> 00:01:27.240
I'm just not into it.

00:01:27.240 --> 00:01:28.649
- Oh my god, I love it so much.

00:01:28.649 --> 00:01:29.482
- [Tony] Do you really?

00:01:29.482 --> 00:01:30.720
- I do too, I love the cold.

00:01:30.720 --> 00:01:31.806
- Do you really, you
love the cold weather?

00:01:31.806 --> 00:01:32.639
- I'm so happy, when it's cold.

00:01:32.639 --> 00:01:35.580
- It makes me so... it feels
fresh. Like a new start.

00:01:35.580 --> 00:01:36.593
- Oh, I can't stand it.

00:01:36.593 --> 00:01:39.540
I remember when I went to Kansas City,

00:01:39.540 --> 00:01:41.610
it was the first winter,
I've ever felt, like,

00:01:41.610 --> 00:01:43.650
really one of, almost the
first time I ever saw snow.

00:01:43.650 --> 00:01:46.980
And I go out to my car
and we had this freeze

00:01:46.980 --> 00:01:49.650
and the windshield was frozen solid.

00:01:49.650 --> 00:01:50.880
And it's got... you can't see through it.

00:01:50.880 --> 00:01:52.470
So I'm like, what the hell am I gonna do?

00:01:52.470 --> 00:01:53.550
What do I do?

00:01:53.550 --> 00:01:55.920
And so, I didn't know
anything about an ice scraper.

00:01:55.920 --> 00:01:57.660
I didn't know you had
to have one of those.

00:01:57.660 --> 00:01:59.520
So I was like, you know what?

00:01:59.520 --> 00:02:00.780
I'm smart.

00:02:00.780 --> 00:02:03.404
I'm gonna get a glass of
warm water, hot water.

00:02:03.404 --> 00:02:04.623
- Oh no.

00:02:04.623 --> 00:02:05.456
- And I'm just gonna pour it on there

00:02:05.456 --> 00:02:07.470
and it'll melt the glass,
melt the ice right off.

00:02:07.470 --> 00:02:08.520
Boom. Put it on there.

00:02:08.520 --> 00:02:10.500
Crack the windshield and everything.

00:02:10.500 --> 00:02:11.333
I was like, oh.

00:02:11.333 --> 00:02:12.450
But that was my first lesson

00:02:12.450 --> 00:02:13.583
into how to deal with the cold weather.

00:02:13.583 --> 00:02:15.150
- I never really thought about that.

00:02:15.150 --> 00:02:17.430
I mean, I guess in Texas
it... There's extreme cold,

00:02:17.430 --> 00:02:19.560
I feel like, and extreme
heat. So I like...

00:02:19.560 --> 00:02:20.993
- This in Kansas City.

00:02:20.993 --> 00:02:21.826
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:02:21.826 --> 00:02:23.040
- Yeah, so during the winter it's frozen.

00:02:23.040 --> 00:02:24.240
- That's why I don't like heat.

00:02:24.240 --> 00:02:26.940
That's, I can't take my skin
off, you know what I'm saying?

00:02:26.940 --> 00:02:28.410
But like, you can like,

00:02:28.410 --> 00:02:30.390
put clothes on and stay warmer.

00:02:30.390 --> 00:02:31.860
- Not on a football field.

00:02:31.860 --> 00:02:32.693
- No.

00:02:32.693 --> 00:02:34.500
- So you were in Kansas City pre-Taylor.

00:02:34.500 --> 00:02:35.440
- Pre-, yeah, oh...

00:02:35.440 --> 00:02:36.390
(audience laughing)

00:02:36.390 --> 00:02:39.450
- Well, same position.
Right. Same thing. Same team.

00:02:39.450 --> 00:02:40.283
- Same team.

00:02:40.283 --> 00:02:42.170
- Did he just break your record, Kelce?

00:02:42.170 --> 00:02:43.070
- He broke my record.

00:02:43.070 --> 00:02:45.060
- Do you have to be bringing that up?

00:02:45.060 --> 00:02:46.624
- Oh, no...

00:02:46.624 --> 00:02:48.614
(audience laughing)

00:02:48.614 --> 00:02:50.266
No, because you tweeted about it.

00:02:50.266 --> 00:02:51.690
You did something about it.

00:02:51.690 --> 00:02:52.710
That's how I know.

00:02:52.710 --> 00:02:55.642
- Yeah. Well, Travis Kelce...

00:02:55.642 --> 00:02:56.767
- You said congratulations.

00:02:56.767 --> 00:02:57.600
- I said congra... Of course.

00:02:57.600 --> 00:02:58.433
- Yeah.

00:02:58.433 --> 00:02:59.266
- He's such a good dude,

00:02:59.266 --> 00:03:01.170
and the whole Taylor Swift thing now.

00:03:01.170 --> 00:03:02.003
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:03:02.003 --> 00:03:03.900
- Is becoming to... I was
in the airport the other day

00:03:03.900 --> 00:03:05.730
and this ten-year-old
girl, comes up to me,

00:03:05.730 --> 00:03:09.180
and I don't, you know, men
usually come up to me, football.

00:03:09.180 --> 00:03:10.440
- Yeah.

00:03:10.440 --> 00:03:12.690
- And occasionally
like, you know, a woman,

00:03:12.690 --> 00:03:15.210
but a ten-year-old girl,
I was like, oh, how cool.

00:03:15.210 --> 00:03:17.757
I'm getting so popular
that a ten-year-old girl

00:03:17.757 --> 00:03:18.590
comes up to me.

00:03:18.590 --> 00:03:19.680
She goes, hi, is your name Tony?

00:03:19.680 --> 00:03:20.820
And I go, yes, it is.

00:03:20.820 --> 00:03:21.870
You know, like maybe (indistinct)

00:03:21.870 --> 00:03:23.430
she goes, do you know Travis Kelce?

00:03:23.430 --> 00:03:24.656
And I'm like...

00:03:24.656 --> 00:03:27.093
(audience laughing)

00:03:27.093 --> 00:03:29.103
- But, I think it's great.

00:03:29.103 --> 00:03:29.936
- My god.

00:03:29.936 --> 00:03:31.500
- That Taylor's done this for the NFL.

00:03:31.500 --> 00:03:33.814
She's brought a whole new
audience. It's been great, yeah.

00:03:33.814 --> 00:03:34.647
- Yeah. Yeah.

00:03:34.647 --> 00:03:36.593
- I will say that, that is true.

00:03:36.593 --> 00:03:38.640
And there's a lot of Swift'ies
out there watching now.

00:03:38.640 --> 00:03:40.320
But I will say, and not because of that,

00:03:40.320 --> 00:03:42.240
but I really got into football this year.

00:03:42.240 --> 00:03:43.950
Like, I finally, I
think I just broke down.

00:03:43.950 --> 00:03:45.330
Because all my friends
and family are into it.

00:03:45.330 --> 00:03:47.190
I'm literally an alone on an island.

00:03:47.190 --> 00:03:49.020
But I am obsessed.

00:03:49.020 --> 00:03:50.880
Like I'm in Fantasy Football League.

00:03:50.880 --> 00:03:51.713
- Oh, I was going to say.

00:03:51.713 --> 00:03:52.620
- I love...

00:03:52.620 --> 00:03:53.453
Do you do Fantasy?

00:03:53.453 --> 00:03:55.740
- I do Fantasy. I do it with my boys.

00:03:55.740 --> 00:03:57.540
My boy River and Nikko.

00:03:57.540 --> 00:03:58.560
We're in a little league and stuff.

00:03:58.560 --> 00:03:59.393
- Oh yeah, we both have a
river. I forgot about that.

00:03:59.393 --> 00:04:00.226
- Yeah. We've got the river.

00:04:00.226 --> 00:04:01.059
- Yeah, that's right.

00:04:01.059 --> 00:04:01.920
Oh my god, I'm obsessed with,

00:04:01.920 --> 00:04:03.570
I almost wish I, are you into football?

00:04:03.570 --> 00:04:05.703
- I really like football.

00:04:06.541 --> 00:04:07.573
I really do.

00:04:07.573 --> 00:04:10.012
I really like marching bands. So I like...

00:04:10.012 --> 00:04:14.986
(audience laughing)

00:04:14.986 --> 00:04:17.640
- Is that not cool to admit?
Wait, are you kidding me?

00:04:17.640 --> 00:04:20.580
The Ohio-Michigan game
and how the Ohio comes in.

00:04:20.580 --> 00:04:21.594
- It's cool.

00:04:21.594 --> 00:04:22.710
- Right.

00:04:22.710 --> 00:04:24.990
- Wait, I literally just
lost my mic pack on that.

00:04:24.990 --> 00:04:26.820
I like... No, I got Rosa.

00:04:26.820 --> 00:04:28.530
I'm putting it back on. I'm so bendy.

00:04:28.530 --> 00:04:31.440
Okay, so wait, talk about
Thursday Night Football.

00:04:31.440 --> 00:04:32.790
What is the show like? It's kind of crazy.

00:04:32.790 --> 00:04:34.740
It's not just football.
Y'all get fun on that.

00:04:34.740 --> 00:04:35.573
- Oh, we do.

00:04:35.573 --> 00:04:36.480
It's like a variety show sometime.

00:04:36.480 --> 00:04:39.540
I mean, we do it, well
the pregame show is pretty

00:04:39.540 --> 00:04:40.800
traditional, like a pregame show,

00:04:40.800 --> 00:04:42.090
we get you ready for the game.

00:04:42.090 --> 00:04:43.980
What to expect, what not to expect.

00:04:43.980 --> 00:04:46.590
We have some segments,
Marshawn Lynch is on there.

00:04:46.590 --> 00:04:47.423
I don't know if you guys know who he is.

00:04:47.423 --> 00:04:48.789
He's pretty crazy.

00:04:48.789 --> 00:04:51.540
He'll do a couple... Where
he, he'll go to like a bar

00:04:51.540 --> 00:04:53.520
or go to a restaurant.

00:04:53.520 --> 00:04:55.980
What else do we do, after the game though?

00:04:55.980 --> 00:04:57.060
It's really cool.

00:04:57.060 --> 00:04:59.370
That's where we bring on,
like, the player of the game.

00:04:59.370 --> 00:05:00.990
So like, Darnay Holmes will be on set.

00:05:00.990 --> 00:05:01.823
- Yeah.

00:05:01.823 --> 00:05:04.710
- We'll shower bazooka brats.

00:05:04.710 --> 00:05:05.543
- [Kelly] Why not?

00:05:05.543 --> 00:05:07.020
- How many can you catch in 30 minutes?

00:05:07.020 --> 00:05:08.850
So it's like more fun
and you're at the game.

00:05:08.850 --> 00:05:12.150
So, the energy, it's electric.
It's just a lot more fun.

00:05:12.150 --> 00:05:13.950
- I love that. That seems so much fun.

00:05:13.950 --> 00:05:15.780
Okay, well before we
do a commercial break,

00:05:15.780 --> 00:05:19.950
we got Tony a special
Kelly Clarkson show merch

00:05:19.950 --> 00:05:20.938
to keep him warm.

00:05:20.938 --> 00:05:22.921
(person laughing)

00:05:22.921 --> 00:05:24.022
This is for you.

00:05:24.022 --> 00:05:25.609
Happy Holidays.

00:05:25.609 --> 00:05:26.442
- I love it.

00:05:26.442 --> 00:05:27.275
No matter what it is.

00:05:27.275 --> 00:05:28.108
- Happy holidays.

00:05:28.108 --> 00:05:30.201
(audience cheering)

00:05:30.201 --> 00:05:32.625
- Oh my goodness.

00:05:32.625 --> 00:05:34.800
- And now, I literally
watch you all the time.

00:05:34.800 --> 00:05:37.590
I was not into Football before,
but now I catch everything.

00:05:37.590 --> 00:05:39.870
I'm even like the NFL plus girl.

00:05:39.870 --> 00:05:41.807
Listen, you're going to look so good.

00:05:41.807 --> 00:05:42.640
- Can I wear this?

00:05:42.640 --> 00:05:43.625
I'm gonna wear this on the set next year.

00:05:43.625 --> 00:05:44.575
- You should wear it.

00:05:44.575 --> 00:05:47.556
(audience cheering)

00:05:47.556 --> 00:05:49.060
- Alright everybody, watch
Thursday Night Football,

00:05:49.060 --> 00:05:51.630
every Thursday starting
at 7:00 pm Eastern.

00:05:51.630 --> 00:05:52.983
Only on Prime video.

